iovascular effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Despite being applied topically for hair loss, 米诺地尔酊 (minoxidil tincture) and 米诺地尔搽剂 (minoxidil liniment) are documented to cause 心动过速 (tachycardia), with evidence noting that 'part of minoxidil is absorbed through the skin' and may lead to cardiovascular side effects such as angina or orthostatic hypotension. This indicates that even non-oral routes of administration for vasodilatory agents can result in clinically significant systemic exposure. Regulatory or clinical guidance should consider these risks, especially in patients with pre-existing heart conditions. [Data: Relationships (15026, 15024); Entities (7654, 7653)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Vasodilator drug class exhibits multiple serious systemic side effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The drug class 血管扩张药物 (vasodilators) is associated with three distinct adverse reactions: 心动过速 (tachycardia), 心排出量增加 (increased cardiac output), and 高肾素血症 (hyperreninemia). These effects are described in the context of interactions with beta-blockers like propranolol (心得安), which can mitigate these responses and thereby enhance antihypertensive efficacy. This triad of side effects reflects the physiological consequences of systemic vasodilation—compensatory increases in heart rate and renin release—and underscores the need for careful management in hypertensive therapy. [Data: Relationships (16110, 16111, 16112); Entities (11825, 15960, 17754)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Tachycardia is a recurrent adverse reaction across diverse drug types\",\n            \"explanation\": \"心动过速 (tachycardia) emerges as a central adverse effect connecting multiple entities: it is reported for 鼻炎通, 镇咳宁含, 鼻炎滴剂, 米诺地尔酊, 米诺地尔搽剂, 血管扩张药物, and even 丁溴东莨菪碱 (scopolamine butylbromide) in unstructured reports from Australian regulatory alerts. This cross-cutting symptom appears in both respiratory, dermatological, and gastrointestinal medica